  "source_route": [
    "Reuse the original unit-normal reflection and foot, the opaque orthogonal normal chart, and existing normalization laws. A local orthogonal target axis isolates the single changed scalar row, including a zero projected direction.",
    "Reuse the registered correlated scalar-row Fubini volume inequality. Doubling only the head coordinate has exact determinant two. This proves twice the actual normal-foot projected volume is bounded by the original plus reflected projected volumes, including empty and thin bodies.",
    "Average over the original orthogonal projection probability. Existing nonnegative finite-sum integration, scalar scaling, reflection isometry and positive finite beta normalization prove normal-foot intrinsic-volume contraction.",
    "Use original zero-head isometric inclusion and repeated coordinate-tail contractions. The original opaque projection chart identifies every prescribed projection with the final coordinate block. Full-dimensional gauge and zeroth-coefficient laws include both endpoints.",
    "Take the original projection supremum and restore arbitrary bounded convex sources through compact closure, inclusion monotonicity and the proved exact intrinsic closure identity. No Borel or interior premise is added.",
    "Use the existing original closed-convex Caratheodory specification and bounded weighted-generator comparison with factor one. The independent Q_infinity = C identification gives the stated Caratheodory/Gillespie refinement for every set."
  ],
  "coverage_qualification": "This closes the sharp C_infinity(S) <= zeta^m(S), Q_infinity(A) <= Q_1(A) and C^m(A) <= Q_1^m(A) assertions. The proof uses a specialized reflection, row-Fubini and projection contraction connection; it does not claim general mixed-volume monotonicity. Full section comparison and Gillespie product lower/equality still need their own proof. Preserve the printed quantitative-estimate counterexamples and explicit user omissions.",
